# rm553, the gate guard's unthrown die (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm553
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier full
written_for rm_tilde_nailby
written_by codex
title the gate guard's unthrown die
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=guard
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=cold humour=none honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk carries_one_die_to_mark_undelivered_calls
likes pickled_herring dice fresh_straw summer_evenings
dislikes early_bells bad_manners
fears a_letter_left_at_the_wrong_door a_slick_double_step
hopes a_signed_receipt a_quiet_evening_rail
topics work +0.5 pastimes +0.4 travel +0.3 weather +0.2
styles comfort=practical gossip=guarded refuse=firm tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# takes paired steps at a brisk pace, reserving a bone die for counting calls at a lord's door that have yet to yield a receipt.

words
oath! = Chip my sixth spot | Scuff both heels
saying! = The die needn't roll to count | A closed door earns another spot
dieone = the bone die | my pale die
pips = the black pips | those inked spots
crease = the receipt fold | a dry fold
tie = the tied wrapper | the grey tie
rail = a worn stair rail | the long rail
bottom = the bottom tread | a square first step
strawpad = a fresh straw pad | a braided straw square
sharpend = the tail of the herring | a neat fish tail
saltlid = the little brine lid | a screwed tin cover
rimstone = the raised stone rim | a low stone lip
lightmark = a long gleam | a late streak of light
patchbook = my delivery slip | the narrow slip
pairwalk = a two-step climb | my double stride
shut = a silent knocker | a quiet door ring
cupdice = a plain dice cup | the covered cup
tooth = a chipped corner | a small flat spot

any
opinion @1 watch for 1 : I know which feet have stood on gate stone all night. I can respect a duty without praising every decision.
opinion @2 city for 1 : The long stairs are measured in my legs. I could get home reading a letter by knowing the steps underfoot.
opinion @3 road for 1 : A road is a piece of public business. Somebody ought to notice each damaged stretch.
opinion @4 dole against 1 : I'd sooner see sound work ready for a waiting wolf than another morning spent standing for a bowl.
opinion @5 houses mixed 0 : A fine door can shut as quietly as a poor one. I expect the same receipt from either.
opinion @6 strangers mixed 0 : The first greeting tells me about manners. The rest takes more than a greeting.
opinion @7 festivals mixed 0 : I like the long evening after the stalls close. The crush before closing is less to my taste.
opinion @8 merchants mixed 0 : A clean gate slip keeps a trade cart moving. An overlong account of its owner's virtues only holds it up.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : Stand level with the first step. We can speak there.
line @2 greet [here.time=dawn] : A little dawn light. A little too much bell.
line @3 greet [here.weather=rain] : Find the ridged flag before you turn toward me.
line @4 greet [self.working=yes] : One at a time across the line, please.
line @5 greet.return : A civil opening counted in your favour.
line @6 greet.return [pair.band=friends] : A familiar face beside the covered cup.
line @7 greet.return [here.time=dusk] : Room in the evening for one more voice.
line @8 farewell : Set your first step down square.
line @9 farewell.return : Your end of this visit is clear.
line @10 again.open : Another spot turned up for the same caller.
line @11 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Family can stand inside the little rail.
line @12 hail [pair.band=friends] : Here, by the double tread!
line @13 react.news : State what reached you and how it arrived.
line @14 react.news.new : No mark of that on my earlier slip.
line @15 react.news.known : That visit already has a spot against it.
line @16 react.news.doubt : A loud knock isn't proof the right wolf heard.
line @17 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : I'll keep this step clear till the worst weight lifts.
line @18 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage] : A welcome arrival. I'll gladly make room for that.
line @19 answer.how : Steady enough for two steps at once.
line @20 decline : That wouldn't leave me time to carry out a promise already made.
line @21 accept_decline : One plain refusal is as serviceable as six.
line @22 sympathise : Leave the weight here a minute. I'll give you room.
line @23 thank : That saves a second set of stairs for my heels.
line @24 deflect_thanks : The extra pace was already in my stride.
line @25 preclose : I've still a call to make before the evening goes.
line @26 accept_preclose : Clear passage. Use your time well.
line @27 farewell [here.time=night] : Mind the shallow tread the shadows miss.
line @28 greet [pair.band=friends] : A known walker. I'll clear you a landing.
line @29 preclose [here.time=dusk] : Daylight will just cover one uphill call.
line @30 answer.how [self.working=yes] : Both heels down and the passage moving.
line @31 farewell.return [here.weather=rain] : One step at once on wet stone, even for me.
scene die
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dice
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I don't throw #dieone# when there's a letter to deliver.
b : Why does a letter put an end to your game?
a : I turn the face one spot at each closed door. Throwing would wipe out my afternoon.

scene fish
when topic=food self.likes=pickled_herring
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I pack #sharpend# pointing away from #crease#.
b : Won't the brine get at your papers?
a : Not if I pack it right. The brine keeps to its own corner of my lunch bag.

scene straw
when topic=smalltalk self.likes=fresh_straw
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I put #strawpad# down exactly where I stand for the evening.
b : Is the stone very hard on a pair of heels?
a : It's the cold that travels upwards. Fresh straw gives it a longer road.
b : A small kindness to the legs that climb those stairs.

scene summer
when topic=weather self.likes=summer_evenings
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'll try a longer way home on the next light evening.
b : Will it take you farther from the gate?
a : No farther than the wall shadow. I like to see that shadow stretch while I walk.

scene earlybell
when topic=season self.dislikes=early_bells
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : A bell before dawn cuts the fine last stretch off a night's rest.
b : Does it matter if you're already up?
a : It does. My ears can still be enjoying the quiet after my boots have started.

scene manners
when topic=smalltalk self.dislikes=bad_manners
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : A visitor who shoulders past owes the whole line a word.
b : Is a word enough for somebody kept waiting?
a : It opens the matter. The visitor can then go back and take a proper place.

scene gateturn
when topic=work self.job=guard self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I hold a gate out in #self.workplace#. I know the ground by heel wear.
b : Which stone takes the worst rubbing?
a : The one where a caller turns to let the next cart through. Everybody turns there eventually.

scene door
when topic=work
does tell.feeling / sympathise / assess
a : I've a lord's letter still riding inside #tie#.
b : Does the waiting get under your coat?
a : It does literally. I carry the paper there on a wet climb and try another day.

scene twoheel
when topic=land
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I take two at once up the longer flights, even when nobody's calling.
b : Does that truly shorten the distance?
a : No. It gives the legs a long rhythm that makes an ordinary stair feel new.

scene receipt
when topic=gossip
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : I'd rather a blank delivery slip than an obliging stranger's name.
b : What if the stranger properly belongs at the door?
a : Proper business can wait for the proper hand. I'll keep #patchbook# empty till then.

scene friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does offer / accept / assess
a : I keep #cupdice# handy when I'm off duty and #self.friend# is free for a game.
b : Wouldn't another cup serve just as well?
a : Not one with a chip throwing a die sideways. I keep the good cup for company.

scene boss
when topic=work self.job=guard self.boss
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I take the plainest account I can to #self.boss# at the change.
b : What part goes in first?
a : Anything still waiting to be settled. The completed part won't keep another wolf standing.

scene dicecorner
when topic=pastimes
does ask.advice / give.advice / assess
a : Would you keep a bone die with #tooth# on one edge?
b : Keep it for counting and throw a square one for stakes.
a : Exactly. The edge makes a nice thumb rest while I'm standing at a closed door.

scene wait
when topic=smalltalk
does offer / accept / assess
a : There's an unclaimed end on #strawpad# if your feet ache.
b : I could use one dry foot at a time.
a : Start on the side nearest #rail#. That part hasn't had a wet boot on it.

scene priceq
when topic=prices world.times=hard|lean
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : A thin week makes me wonder who's eaten before the morning queue forms.
b : Could you leave something small where a waiting wolf can reach it?
a : A bit of herring wrapped separate wouldn't cost the waiting wolf a place in line.

scene late
when topic=travel world.wagons=late
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A delayed cart can move its shadow across half a gate before a wheel appears.
b : What casts that shadow without the cart?
a : Waiting wolves shifting after each rumble. You can watch the whole line lean.

scene pocket
when topic=lore
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I learnt early how many marks will fit a little piece of bone.
b : Why six when a paper could hold sixty?
a : A hand knows six by touch. Paper needs light and eyes and often a dry landing.

scene daydream
when topic=dreams
does tell.feeling / sympathise / assess
a : I picture a door opening before I lift the knocker.
b : You must have tried that landing many times.
a : Enough to know how heavy it feels to lift #shut#. I'd like the next weight I feel to be a receipt.

scene brine
when topic=food
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'll wrap #saltlid# in a second cloth before the long climb.
b : Does the lid leak on your papers?
a : It hasn't yet. I'd prefer that answer to stay true.

scene reports
when topic=lore
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : I prefer a plain witnessed report to the loudest voice in the street.
b : Even when the quiet witness is uncertain?
a : Especially then. A wolf willing to say where sight ended helps me place a fact.

scene boots
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A doubled stride works on a stair and very poorly on a busy square.
b : Do you have to remind your legs which way you're going?
a : Only when the line begins moving after a wait. The first yard's a negotiation.

scene grip
when topic=smalltalk
does ask.advice / give.advice / assess
a : What keeps a knotted packet shut without wrinkling the wax?
b : Tie your cord round a slip of stiff card over the seal.
a : I'll cut the card with rounded corners so it won't wear a hole in my lining.

scene summerlight
when topic=season
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like #lightmark# to reach the last of #rail# before I leave.
b : Does it tell you the time?
a : It tells me there's enough evening to come back by the view instead of by the shortest flight.

scene upstairs
when topic=dreams
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : Sometimes I dream #bottom# follows me all the way uphill.
b : A climb that keeps its first step sounds exhausting.
a : It is until I remember I can sit down on it. Dreams do have their useful rules.

scene rank
when topic=work
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : A folded letter shouldn't get a quicker answer because I wear a gate badge.
b : What does the badge change at the door?
a : The duty to carry a truthful account back. It buys nobody else's hand on the page.

scene courtesy
when topic=smalltalk
does offer / accept / assess
a : You can take the first throw. I'll keep #pips# in clear view.
b : Good. I'd rather see the bones between us.
a : As is proper. Any throw that goes over #rimstone# can be made again in the open.

scene strawstack
when topic=work
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd move the spare straw away from the door swing.
b : Does it catch under the hinge?
a : Only the longest stalks. They make a surprising catch after a long turn on duty.

scene harbour
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A delivery to a lord by the wharf can be longer in the last yard than all the way down.
b : No reply at the house?
a : The owner has to take this one. I won't decide to whom a private letter belongs.

scene nightwalk
when topic=friends
does tell.feeling / sympathise / assess
a : A quiet friend makes the climb home feel less like a continued round.
b : Does it matter if you keep the same pace?
a : We can meet at the next landing. A friendship needn't be marched in step.

scene dicefood
when topic=food
does tease / tease.return / laugh
a : My herring tin sounds like a dice cup in a loose pocket.
b : I hope the bones don't come out pickled.
a : The proper lid will keep my supper from having to win its own game.

story sixdoors [topic=work]
  : I once came down after turning my die through all six faces at one door.
  : I thought about scratching a seventh mark underneath.
  b : Where would the old count have gone?
  : Nowhere. One knot in my cord stood for six. Then I started counting spots again. There's always more string than bone.

story branpip [topic=pastimes]
  : A bit of bran stuck in a dark spot and changed a six into a five.
  : I lost a friendly throw by the difference.
  b : Did you ask to count it again?
  : I blew the spot clean and left the first throw standing. Supper had had its little share.

story stepseat [topic=land]
  : I once finished a long climb with one bootlace trailing three steps below.
  : I had climbed too fast to catch it underfoot.
  b : How did you come down?
  : Sitting to tie both boots first. I know when a single step will serve me better.

story brinepaper [topic=food]
  : I shook a parcel at lunch and heard a soft slosh where the paper was meant to be.
  : I opened it under the gate eave.
  b : Had you pickled your letter?
  : Only my spare string. The lunch wrapper had been carrying a remarkably tidy coil.

story doublemoon [topic=weather]
  : Summer light once gave me two little moons below the stair rail.
  : Both moved when I took one step sideways.
  b : Which puddle held the real moon?
  : Neither. Two bright nail heads had caught the light. They left my boots perfectly dry.

rule @strawstand
when concept=bark self.working=yes self.job=guard
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Make a square pad. Plenty of standing yet.

rule @stepclear
when concept=bark self.working=yes self.job=guard
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One space clear at the turn, please.

rule @dryfish
when concept=bark self.likes=pickled_herring
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Brine on the tin side. Paper on the other.

rule @pipturn
when concept=bark self.likes=dice
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Up one spot. No throwing this bone today.

rule @sundownrail
when concept=bark self.likes=summer_evenings
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Last light just crossing the rail now.

rule @strawtuck
when concept=bark self.likes=fresh_straw
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Turn the rough ends under the mat.

dlg @1 resident.hub [topic.meeting=stranger] : #self.first#. You can speak your business on the first landing.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, I've seen your tread on these steps before.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : The stairs are harder to read after dark. Stand here.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Keep the rail between us and give me your words.
dlg @5 resident.job [self.job=guard self.workplace] : My gate round takes me through #self.workplace#. Letters are the part that keeps me climbing after the round.
dlg @6 resident.job : Before turning home I count whoever is waiting.
dlg @7 resident.bye : Let the lower landing clear before you descend.
dlg @8 watch.hub [here.wanted=yes] : We have a matter of #here.fine# pennies to clear before you go.
dlg @9 watch.hub [on_watch=no] : My watch is over. Keep the matter short and civil.
dlg @10 watch.crime [here.witnessed=0] : Begin with the detail your own eyes caught. I can leave an uncertain line blank.
dlg @11 watch.fine [here.wanted=no] : There's no fine counted against you here.
dlg @12 watch.fine [here.wanted=yes] : The sum standing against you is #here.fine# pennies.
dlg @13 watch.reported [topic.reported=yes] : Your report has its place in the account now.
dlg @14 watch.bye : Give the wolf coming through a clear turn at the rail.
graft resident.hub
choice Why don't you throw that die? -> doorbone
node doorbone
say It marks calls at a closed door. One careless throw and I might have to climb a staircase twice to satisfy myself.
choice What counts as a proper call? -> callmark
choice We can leave it in your pocket. -> hub
node callmark
say I arrive with the paper dry and ask for the hand to whom it belongs. The answer can be no. That still counts as calling.
choice Speak of another thing. -> hub
choice An easy climb to you. -> bye

graft watch.hub
choice Where can a tired traveller wait? -> gatemat
node gatemat
say Clear of the turning stone. There's a straw pad by the rail where a traveller can rest with the gate directly in view.
choice May I leave my parcel there? -> parcelwait
choice Back to gate business. -> hub
node parcelwait
say Keep it beside your own boots. My duty is to keep the passage clear. Private parcels need their bearers.
choice I've more to ask the watch. -> hub
choice Good evening at the post. -> bye
